00:22:57,367 --> 00:22:59,119
COP 1 : That 's the guy . COP 2 : Was he ?

260
00:22:59,247 --> 00:23:01,556
COP 3 : Yeah , that 's the guy who arrested Lecter .

261
00:23:01,647 --> 00:23:03,160
COP 4 : I thought he retired .

262
00:23:03,247 --> 00:23:06,045
COP 5 : The son of a bitch just about gutted him .

263
00:23:11,087 --> 00:23:14,397
Mrs. Leeds and Mrs. Jacobi were the primary targets .

264
00:23:14,567 --> 00:23:17,798
The others were killed just to complete his fantasy .

265
00:23:17,927 --> 00:23:20,999
will : I know that might be hard to accept given what you saw ...

266
00:23:21,087 --> 00:23:23,043
but this was not random .

267
00:23:23,127 --> 00:23:26,915
This wasn 't some killing frenzy . He was never out of control .

268
00:23:27,647 --> 00:23:31,003
These attacks were organised , the women carefully chosen .

269
00:23:31,087 --> 00:23:33,601
We don 't know how he 's choosing them , or why .

270
00:23:33,687 --> 00:23:36,281
They lived in different states and never met .

271
00:23:36,367 --> 00:23:37,959
But there is some connection .

272
00:23:38,287 --> 00:23:41,324
There 's some common factor , and that 's the key .

273
00:23:41,727 --> 00:23:44,366
Find out what that is , and we 'll save lives .

274
00:23:44,447 --> 00:23:47,644
'Cause this one is gonna go on and on ...

275
00:23:47,807 --> 00:23:50,401
until we get smart or we get lucky .

276
00:23:51,967 --> 00:23:53,446
He won 't stop .

277
00:23:54,607 --> 00:23:58,202
- Why not ? - Because it makes him God .

278
00:23:59,047 --> 00:24:00,958
Would you give that up ?

279
00:24:02,527 --> 00:24:06,122
You asked about the dog . Last night a vet called us .

280
00:24:06,327 --> 00:24:08,887
Leeds and his oldest boy brought the dog in ...

281
00:24:08,967 --> 00:24:10,605
the afternoon before they were killed .

282
00:24:10,847 --> 00:24:13,042
Had a puncture wound to its abdomen .

283
00:24:13,127 --> 00:24:14,799
The vet had to put it down .

284
00:24:14,887 --> 00:24:17,117
Was it wearing a collar with the address on it ?

285
00:24:17,207 --> 00:24:18,242
No .

286
00:24:19,367 --> 00:24:22,165
- Did the Jacobis have a dog ? - No dog .

287
00:24:22,247 --> 00:24:24,124
They found a litter box in the basement ...

288
00:24:24,207 --> 00:24:26,482
cat droppings in it , no cat .

289
00:24:28,327 --> 00:24:31,797
If the cat was attacked , the Jacobis may have buried it .

290
00:24:32,807 --> 00:24:35,401
Ask Birmingham to check that backyard .

291
00:24:35,487 --> 00:24:37,682
And tell them to use a methane probe , it 's faster .

292
00:24:37,767 --> 00:24:39,678
[ Telephone rings ]

293
00:24:41,287 --> 00:24:45,405
Yeah. lt 's for you .

294
00:24:46,687 --> 00:24:47,961
Crawford .

295
00:24:51,687 --> 00:24:53,917
Carl , you 're the light of my life .

296
00:24:54,127 --> 00:24:55,606
Would it hold up in court ?

297
00:24:55,847 --> 00:24:57,519
Okay . Great work .

298
00:24:59,167 --> 00:25:02,842
They found a print on Mrs. Leeds ' eye . Partial thumb .

299
00:25:04,247 --> 00:25:06,602
Besides that , there 's nothing else to tell you .

300
00:25:06,687 --> 00:25:07,676
Thank you for your time .

301
00:25:07,767 --> 00:25:09,359
commissioner : I can 't answer more questions .

302
00:25:09,447 --> 00:25:11,483
Will Graham ! Remember me ?

303
00:25:12,247 --> 00:25:16,035
Freddy Lounds. I covered the Lecter case for the Tattler .

304
00:25:16,247 --> 00:25:18,124
- Did the paperback . - Yeah , I remember .

305
00:25:18,207 --> 00:25:20,402
When did they bring you in ? What 've you got ?

306
00:25:20,847 --> 00:25:24,123
You think the Tooth Fairy will be bigger than Lecter ?

307
00:25:24,207 --> 00:25:26,437
I mean , he 's already beaten Lecter 's score- -

308
00:25:26,607 --> 00:25:29,485
You write lying shit , and the Tattler is an asswipe !

309
00:25:29,567 --> 00:25:31,398
You stay away from me .

310
00:25:31,727 --> 00:25:33,365
Get away , Lounds .

311
00:25:35,007 --> 00:25:36,918
How about an exclusive ?

312
00:25:39,567 --> 00:25:41,159
Sorry about that .

313
00:25:41,287 --> 00:25:44,324
That guy snuck into the hospital and took those pictures of me .

314
00:25:44,407 --> 00:25:46,477
Remember ? With the tubes hanging out of me ?

315
00:25:46,567 --> 00:25:47,841
Forget that prick .

316
00:25:48,167 --> 00:25:49,600
CRAWFORD : Give yourself some credit .

317
00:25:49,687 --> 00:25:51,325
When we catch the Tooth Fairy ...

318
00:25:51,407 --> 00:25:53,967
that print plus his teeth will burn him .

319
00:25:54,407 --> 00:25:55,806
You did that , Will .

320
00:25:55,887 --> 00:25:57,843
That evidence was there , Jack .

321
00:25:58,327 --> 00:26:02,115
- lt was there for anyone to see . - But nobody else did .

322
00:26:02,207 --> 00:26:04,482
All I 'm sayin ' is , that was very good work .

323
00:26:04,567 --> 00:26:07,206
No , good work would be seeing it all the way through ...

324
00:26:07,287 --> 00:26:08,686
and catching the guy .

325
00:26:08,767 --> 00:26:12,043
And I can 't do that . I did what you asked me to do .

326
00:26:12,647 --> 00:26:14,160
I 'm going home .

327
00:26:15,527 --> 00:26:18,087
I don 't even have any idea who this guy is .

328
00:26:18,167 --> 00:26:21,443
What I just gave them was broad strokes . He 's got no face to me .

329
00:26:21,527 --> 00:26:24,325
That 's what you said about Garrett Hobbs , remember ?

330
00:26:24,407 --> 00:26:26,875
- And you figured him out . - No , I didn 't .

331
00:26:26,967 --> 00:26:29,606
- You didn 't ? - No , I was stuck on Hobbs .

332
00:26:31,527 --> 00:26:32,880
I had help .

333
00:26:37,207 --> 00:26:38,606
From Lecter .

334
00:26:40,967 --> 00:26:42,082
will : Yeah .

335
00:26:46,807 --> 00:26:49,879
Jack , don 't play games with me . Don 't do it .

336
00:26:50,967 --> 00:26:52,685
Just tell me what 's on your mind .

337
00:26:52,767 --> 00:26:56,043
I 'm saying maybe we 've got a resource we should look into .

338
00:26:56,127 --> 00:26:57,560
is that what this was about ?

339
00:26:57,647 --> 00:26:59,603
Did you just want to ask me that all along ?

340
00:26:59,687 --> 00:27:01,837
Don 't get mad at me . I 'm just doing my job .

341
00:27:01,927 --> 00:27:04,202
If you know a better shortcut , let me know it .

342
00:27:04,287 --> 00:27:06,642
If you think there 's any chance he 'll talk to me ...

343
00:27:06,727 --> 00:27:08,285
I 'll go myself .

344
00:27:09,727 --> 00:27:13,800
If you can 't handle it , God knows I 'd understand that .

345
00:27:20,727 --> 00:27:24,515
CHlLTON : As a research subject , Lecter has proven most disappointing .

346
00:27:25,047 --> 00:27:28,244
He 's simply impenetrable to psychological testing .

347
00:27:28,527 --> 00:27:30,995
Rorschach , Thematic Apperception .

348
00:27:31,327 --> 00:27:33,602
He folds them into origami .

349
00:27:34,527 --> 00:27:35,880
CHlLTON : As you see .

350
00:27:37,047 --> 00:27:39,242
So you can imagine the stir your little visit ...

351
00:27:39,327 --> 00:27:41,283
is causing among my staff , Mr. Graham .

352
00:27:42,727 --> 00:27:44,877
If you 'd care to share some insights- -

353
00:27:44,967 --> 00:27:48,039
Dr. Chilton , I 'm sorry , I 've got a 4 : 1 7 flight back to Atlanta .

354
00:27:48,127 --> 00:27:49,446
Of course .

355
00:27:52,567 --> 00:27:55,206
Tell me , when you saw Lecter 's murders ...

356
00:27:55,287 --> 00:27:56,845
their style , so to speak ...

357
00:27:56,927 --> 00:28:00,237
were you able , perhaps , to reconstruct his fantasies ?

358
00:28:00,327 --> 00:28:03,160
And , if so , did you jot down any impressions ?

359
00:28:03,247 --> 00:28:04,282
will : No .

360
00:28:11,527 --> 00:28:13,245
Let me be frank , Mr. Graham .

361
00:28:13,327 --> 00:28:17,479
The first analysis of Lecter will be a publisher 's wet dream .

362
00:28:17,567 --> 00:28:20,081
I 'd give you full credit , of course .

363
00:28:23,727 --> 00:28:27,117
Damn it , man . You must have some advice . You caught him .

364
00:28:27,207 --> 00:28:28,765
What was your trick ?

365
00:28:30,007 --> 00:28:31,679
I let him kill me .

366
00:28:32,847 --> 00:28:36,203
[ Door slams shut loudly and locks ]

367
00:28:49,007 --> 00:28:52,682
[ Suspenseful instrumental music ]

368
00:29:23,167 --> 00:29:26,603
LECTER : That 's the same atrocious aftershave you wore in court .

369
00:29:28,447 --> 00:29:30,085
I keep getting it for Christmas .

370
00:29:30,167 --> 00:29:34,160
LECTER : Christmas , yes . Did you get my card ?

371
00:29:35,527 --> 00:29:36,755
I got it , thank you .

372
00:29:36,847 --> 00:29:40,044
LECTER : So nice of the Bureau 's crime lab to forward that .

373
00:29:41,127 --> 00:29:43,880
They wouldn 't give me your home address .

374
00:29:45,087 --> 00:29:47,681
Dr. Bloom sent me your article on surgical addiction ...

375
00:29:47,767 --> 00:29:50,122
in the Journal of Forensic Psychiatry .

376
00:29:50,207 --> 00:29:51,196
LECTER : And ?

377
00:29:52,047 --> 00:29:54,515
Very interesting , even to a layman .

378
00:29:59,407 --> 00:30:01,398
You say you 're a layman .

379
00:30:08,407 --> 00:30:12,116
But it was you who caught me . Wasn 't it , Will ?

380
00:30:13,887 --> 00:30:17,277
LECTER : Do you know how you did it ? will : I got lucky .

381
00:30:18,127 --> 00:30:20,402
I don 't think you believe that .

382
00:30:21,367 --> 00:30:23,676
It 's in the transcript . What does it matter now ?

383
00:30:23,767 --> 00:30:25,997
It doesn 't matter to me , Will .

384
00:30:26,127 --> 00:30:28,402
I need your advice , Dr. Lecter .

385
00:30:30,687 --> 00:30:32,837
LECTER : Birmingham and Atlanta .

386
00:30:33,487 --> 00:30:36,604
You want to know how he 's choosing them , don 't you ?

387
00:30:36,727 --> 00:30:39,525
I thought you 'd have ideas . I want you to tell me them .

388
00:30:39,607 --> 00:30:40,881
Why should I ?

389
00:30:40,967 --> 00:30:42,286
There are things you don 't have .

390
00:30:42,367 --> 00:30:44,927
Research materials . Maybe even computer access .

391
00:30:45,007 --> 00:30:46,520
I 'd speak to the Chief of Staff .

392
00:30:46,807 --> 00:30:48,479
Yes , Dr. Chilton .

393
00:30:49,767 --> 00:30:51,405
Gruesome , isn 't he ?

394
00:30:51,487 --> 00:30:55,560
He fumbles at your head like a freshman pulling at panties .

395
00:30:56,807 --> 00:30:58,365
If you recall , Will ...

396
00:30:58,447 --> 00:31:00,802
our last collaboration ended rather messily .

397
00:31:03,447 --> 00:31:06,007
You 'd get to see the file on this case .

398
00:31:06,247 --> 00:31:09,637
- And there 's another reason . - l 'm all ears .

399
00:31:10,287 --> 00:31:12,596
I thought you might enjoy the challenge .

400
00:31:12,727 --> 00:31:15,525
Find out if you 're smarter than the person I 'm looking for .

401
00:31:16,687 --> 00:31:20,043
[ Slow , ominous instrumental music ]

402
00:31:22,567 --> 00:31:26,162
Then , by implication , you think you 're smarter than I am ...

403
00:31:26,247 --> 00:31:28,317
since it was you who caught me .

404
00:31:28,447 --> 00:31:30,244
I know I 'm not smarter than you .

405
00:31:30,327 --> 00:31:32,045
Then how did you catch me ?

406
00:31:32,247 --> 00:31:34,681
You had disadvantages .

407
00:31:35,007 --> 00:31:36,725
What disadvantages ?

408
00:31:37,207 --> 00:31:38,686
You 're insane .

409
00:31:43,767 --> 00:31:45,803
You 're very tanned , Will .

410
00:31:46,047 --> 00:31:49,483
And your hands are so rough . Not like a cop 's hands anymore .

411
00:31:49,567 --> 00:31:52,559
And that shaving lotion is something a child would select .

412
00:31:52,647 --> 00:31:55,605
Has a little ship on the bottle , does it not ?

413
00:31:56,247 --> 00:31:59,080
And how is young Josh and the lovely Molly ?

414
00:31:59,887 --> 00:32:02,196
They 're always in my thoughts , you know .

415
00:32:02,287 --> 00:32:04,198
You will not persuade me with appeals ...

416
00:32:04,287 --> 00:32:05,686
to my intellectual vanity .

417
00:32:05,767 --> 00:32:07,519
I don 't think I 'll persuade you at all .

418
00:32:07,607 --> 00:32:09,325
You 'll either do it or you won 't .

419
00:32:09,407 --> 00:32:11,557
LECTER : is that the case file ? will : Yes .

420
00:32:11,927 --> 00:32:13,076
With photos ?

421
00:32:13,167 --> 00:32:15,237
Let me keep them , and I might consider it .

422
00:32:15,407 --> 00:32:16,317
No .

423
00:32:19,487 --> 00:32:21,398
Do you dream much , Will ?

424
00:32:21,487 --> 00:32:22,966
Goodbye , Dr. Lecter .

425
00:32:23,047 --> 00:32:26,198
You haven 't threatened to take away my books yet !

426
00:32:26,367 --> 00:32:28,278
Give me the file , then !

427
00:32:29,767 --> 00:32:32,042
And I 'll tell you what I think .

428
00:32:34,567 --> 00:32:36,922
I 'll need one hour . And privacy .

429
00:32:43,407 --> 00:32:45,637
Just like old times , Will ?

430
00:32:45,727 --> 00:32:49,083
[ Suspenseful instrumental music ]

431
00:33:14,367 --> 00:33:16,562
LECTER : This is a very shy boy , Will .

432
00:33:17,087 --> 00:33:18,759
I 'd love to meet him .

433
00:33:18,847 --> 00:33:21,805
Have you considered that he is disfigured ...

434
00:33:21,887 --> 00:33:23,923
or that he may believe he is disfigured ?

435
00:33:24,007 --> 00:33:25,486
Yeah , the mirrors .

436
00:33:25,567 --> 00:33:27,444
Notice he smashes all the mirrors ...

437
00:33:27,527 --> 00:33:29,563
not just enough to get the pieces he wants .

438
00:33:29,647 --> 00:33:31,842
And , of course , those shards in their eyes ...

439
00:33:31,927 --> 00:33:33,201
so he can see himself there .

440
00:33:33,327 --> 00:33:34,476
That 's interesting .

441
00:33:34,567 --> 00:33:36,637
No , it 's not . You thought of it before .

442
00:33:37,247 --> 00:33:38,999
I had considered it .

443
00:33:39,127 --> 00:33:41,163
- What about the women ? - Dead ?

444
00:33:41,247 --> 00:33:42,680
Mere puppets .

445
00:33:42,807 --> 00:33:46,004
You need to see them living , the way they caught his eye .

446
00:33:46,327 --> 00:33:47,476
That 's impossible .

447
00:33:47,567 --> 00:33:49,239
Almost . Not quite .

448
00:33:50,887 --> 00:33:52,878
What were the yards like ?

449
00:33:53,887 --> 00:33:57,766
Big backyards , fenced , some hedges . Why ?

450
00:33:58,167 --> 00:33:59,600
Because if this pilgrim ...

451
00:33:59,687 --> 00:34:01,678
feels a special relationship with the moon ...

452
00:34:01,767 --> 00:34:04,440
he might like to go outside and look at it .

453
00:34:04,527 --> 00:34:06,358
You ever seen blood in the moonlight ?

454
00:34:06,447 --> 00:34:08,324
It appears quite black .

455
00:34:08,527 --> 00:34:11,883
If one were nude , say , it 'd be better to have ...

456
00:34:11,967 --> 00:34:13,798
outdoor privacy for that sort of thing .

457
00:34:14,647 --> 00:34:17,320
You think the yards are a factor when he selects victims ?

458
00:34:17,407 --> 00:34:18,396
Yes .

459
00:34:18,807 --> 00:34:22,083
And there will be more of them , of course . Victims .

460
00:34:23,327 --> 00:34:25,602
You 'll be wanting lots of these little chinwags ...

461
00:34:25,687 --> 00:34:27,325
- l take it . - l might not have time .

462
00:34:27,407 --> 00:34:28,601
I do .

463
00:34:28,807 --> 00:34:30,286
I have oodles .

464
00:34:30,367 --> 00:34:32,323
I need your opinion now .

465
00:34:32,407 --> 00:34:33,999
Then here 's one :

466
00:34:34,487 --> 00:34:37,320
You stink of fear under that cheap lotion .

467
00:34:37,807 --> 00:34:40,958
You stink of fear , Will , but you 're not a coward !

468
00:34:42,487 --> 00:34:44,398
You fear me , but still you came here .

469
00:34:44,487 --> 00:34:47,843
You fear this shy boy , yet still you seek him out .

470
00:34:50,727 --> 00:34:52,797
Don 't you understand , Will ?

471
00:34:53,247 --> 00:34:56,125
You caught me because we 're very much alike .

472
00:34:57,687 --> 00:34:59,120
Without our imaginations ...

473
00:34:59,207 --> 00:35:01,926
we 'd be like all those other poor dullards .

474
00:35:06,167 --> 00:35:09,125
Fear is the price of our instrument .

475
00:35:09,407 --> 00:35:11,284
But I can help you bear it .

476
00:35:11,327 --> 00:35:14,285
[ Dramatic instrumental music ]

477
00:35:22,407 --> 00:35:23,920
- You getting his face ? - Yeah .

478
00:35:24,007 --> 00:35:25,406
Okay , you got it ?

479
00:35:25,807 --> 00:35:27,525
All right , let 's get the fuck out of here .

480
00:35:28,367 --> 00:35:29,595
CRAWFORD : Sure you 're okay ?

481
00:35:29,687 --> 00:35:31,200
Yeah , I 'm okay .

482
00:35:31,447 --> 00:35:34,166
CRAWFORD : What do you think he meant by " see them living " ?

483
00:35:34,247 --> 00:35:36,681
I don 't know , maybe nothing .

484
00:35:36,807 --> 00:35:39,037
It 's hard to separate his bullshit .

485
00:35:39,127 --> 00:35:41,641
But I 'm gonna make another pass at the Leeds ' house .

486
00:36:22,607 --> 00:36:24,245
[ Vaudeville piano music ]

487
00:36:29,607 --> 00:36:31,040
[ Duchess whines ]

488
00:36:32,247 --> 00:36:33,999
CHARLES : All right , Duchess , doll . That 's it .

489
00:36:34,087 --> 00:36:36,043
Show me what you can do .

490
00:36:37,407 --> 00:36:41,366
Who 's that ? Get them , Duchess . Get them , Duch ! Go get them !

491
00:36:42,087 --> 00:36:43,759
Go get them , girl !

492
00:36:44,007 --> 00:36:44,883
Okay .

493
00:36:44,967 --> 00:36:46,241
CHARLES : And action !

494
00:36:46,327 --> 00:36:48,158
Charles ! What are you doing ?

495
00:36:49,047 --> 00:36:49,843
CHARLES : Hey , gang .

496
00:36:49,927 --> 00:36:51,155
valerie : You crazy man .

497
00:36:51,247 --> 00:36:53,158
CHARLES : How is everybody doing ?

498
00:36:53,247 --> 00:36:54,839
valerie : Just home from the store .

499
00:36:54,927 --> 00:36:56,519
susie : Hi , Daddy . CHARLES : That 's my girl .

500
00:36:56,607 --> 00:36:58,837
SEAN : Hi , Daddy . CHARLES : Hi , honey . Billy ?

501
00:36:58,927 --> 00:36:59,916
Hi , Dad .

502
00:37:00,007 --> 00:37:01,440
CHARLES : And sweetie ?

503
00:37:01,527 --> 00:37:04,564
I am not ready for my close-up , Mr. DeMille .

504
00:37:04,887 --> 00:37:07,003
What do you think ?

505
00:37:07,967 --> 00:37:10,925
Get closer . Get closer . Little closer .

506
00:37:11,607 --> 00:37:14,201
I think we 'd better put these kids to bed early tonight .

507
00:37:14,287 --> 00:37:16,642
valerie : They seem tired . Don 't you think ?

508
00:37:17,607 --> 00:37:19,757
CHARLES : Here we are at the pool party .

509
00:37:19,847 --> 00:37:21,565
What are you doing ? Stop it !

510
00:37:21,647 --> 00:37:23,717
You stop it ! I 'm telling my mother on you .

511
00:37:23,807 --> 00:37:25,479
CHARLES : Now I get my kiss ?

512
00:37:25,567 --> 00:37:29,526
- All right , you want a kiss ? - I want one . The romantic kind .

513
00:37:29,607 --> 00:37:30,881
